      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: hydrate local account identity from bird transport",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nThe web UI showed the seeded `@steipete` placeholder — handle, display name, **and avatar** — whenever the **bird** transport was active. `hydrateProfilesFromX` only ran under the `xurl` transport and bailed out early in local/bird mode, so the seeded default account was never corrected to the authenticated user.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Correct `acct_primary` + `profile_me` from `bird whoami` (handle, name, `external_user_id`) when xurl is unavailable but bird is authenticated.\n- Parse the display name that bird prints as `@handle (Display Name)`.\n- Treat a **changed handle as an identity change even when `bird whoami` omits a numeric id** (`BirdAuthenticatedAccount.id` is optional). On any identity change, reset `external_user_id` (instead of coalescing) and clear the seeded `avatar_url` so no field from the prior account lingers on the new handle. The UI then falls back to initials — bird whoami cannot supply an avatar.\n\n## Usage\n\nHydration stays an explicit, idempotent command (no new startup side effects):\n\n```bash\nbirdclaw import hydrate-profiles   # after init, or after switching bird accounts\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nAgainst a real bird-authenticated setup (ids redacted), in a throwaway `BIRDCLAW_HOME`:\n\n```\n$ bird whoami\n📍 Safari\n🙋 @martintrojer (Martin Trojer)\n🪪 <user-id>\n⚙️ graphql\n\n$ birdclaw init          # seeds the @steipete placeholder\n# BEFORE hydrate:\n#   accounts: handle=@steipete  name=Peter  external_user_id=25401953\n#   profiles: avatar=https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1131851609774985216/OcsssQ9J.png  (steipete's real photo)\n\n$ birdclaw import hydrate-profiles\n{ ok: true, hydratedProfiles: 0, hydratedAccount: true,\n  reason: 'xurl not installed. local mode active.' }\n\n# AFTER hydrate:\n#   accounts: handle=@martintrojer  name=Martin Trojer  external_user_id=<user-id>\n#   profiles: avatar=NULL   (falls back to initials, no longer the wrong photo)\n```\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- I intentionally did **not** wire this into `birdclaw serve` startup to avoid running a `bird whoami` subprocess on every server boot. Happy to add an opt-in hook if you'd prefer the UI to self-correct.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nRan tests — `bird.test.ts` + `profile-hydration.test.ts`, 39 passing (includes coverage for the idless changed-handle path and for preserving the id/avatar when the handle is unchanged).",
